WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
a tiny woman against the hulking alien  nightmare a cgi bear that looks  absolutely unbearable some breadheads  are really gunning for prey  by far the biggest complaint among fans  is the controversial redesign of the  predator which portrays the creature in  a decidedly more monstrous form than  we're used to dubbed the feral predator  it's an ancestor to the bees seen  fighting arnold schwarzenegger's dutch  in the original film 300 years after the  events of prey director dan trachtenberg  told digital spy i wanted to make this  version of the predator so much more  feral and ferocious and animalistic from  its movements to its silhouettes and its  design while trachtenberg's explanation  makes sense some predator fans have  responded negatively to the new look  which is revealed during an action scene  midway through the film you don't need  to look further than the comments  section of the fan website avp galaxy to  see the disdain many have for the design  for instance one user said carol's  weapons were interesting and it was fun  watching him on screen my one gripe is  that it wasn't crazy about the face  redesign it was just okay for me similar  sentiments appear in various comment  circles across the web though the new  look does have several fans one user is  quoted as saying prey is a solid  predator movie predator redesign seemed  unnecessary but didn't bother me way  better than expected  the predator scene in prey lives up to  the species storied reputation the big  guy hunts and kills a rattlesnake a wolf  a bear a group of comanches and a whole  squad of french trappers in brutal  fashion these scenes offer some of the  best action of the entire predator  franchise as the alien baddie utilizes  an assortment of unique weapons and  abilities to take out his foes perhaps  that's why some fans were left feeling  short-changed at the monster's demise  following his trail of carnage the  hunter chases naru who stole his mask in  a previous scene into the forest and  eventually becomes stuck in some mud he  disappears below the surface but manages  to pull himself out of the trap long  enough to aim his arrow launcher at  naru's head unaware that the clever  warrior has placed his mask on a nearby  tree  this is as far as you go  no more  [Music]  this is it  our antagonist can only tilt his head in  confusion before an arrow streaks  through his skull killing him instantly  a twitter user noted the predator dies  in what i think is the dumbest way for a  predator to die it would be a badass  kill if he didn't stand there looking  all osh for a few good seconds  another complaint about prey among fans  is the predator's inability to kill a  young woman with minimal combat  experience one user made a composite  image of the entire cast of the original  predator film standing next to naru  indicating that it took an entire squad  of trained soldiers to take down the  original monster but only a single  inexperienced warrior to succeed in the  latest film one could argue the point of  naru's character arc is to show the  merits of brains over brawn and  outwitting an interstellar killing  machine that isn't convincing enough for  some including one twitter user who  states in this movie the predator one  punch kills a 1 000 pound grizzly but  can't strangle the 110 pound protag even  when it has its hand around her neck one  could also point out that a theme of the  entire original predator film is brains  over brawn dutch is the last one  standing because he realizes that the  combat experience and physical might of  his team are no match for the kind of  clever strategy that both he and naru  rely on in their climactic battles  prey is not a perfect film there's  plenty to love but this predator prequel  has some glaring issues notably the  wonky cgi many of the animals in the  movie look a little off especially  during the bear fight even fans who like  the film point out that some of the  visual effects in the sequence are  simply not up to modern blockbuster  standards one critic said a couple of  intro shots of the bear were not very  good later on when the bear and predator  were fighting was much much better but  you can tell they were like this part  doesn't matter all that much but this  next part will be in the trailer it was  a little rough another tweeted prey was  basically what if the power rangers  movie had very bad cgi though that same  user went on to praise the action scenes  overall they clearly had no love for the  distracting special effects  nauru is largely seen as a misfit by her  fellow tribesmen who don't support her  rebellious ways in fact except for her  brother tabe no one steps up to support  nauru or her quest to become a great  hunter  who invited you  we won't be gone long enough to need a  cook  but the understatement to this aspect is  one of the reasons some critics praised  prey with one noting a subtle approach  to the arc of nauru is appreciated as  the filmmakers rarely resort to forced  antagonism via the tribe's people to  make their point some fans don't agree  including the hosts of the angry movie  review who cite the scene in which one  of the men in nauru's tribe orders her  to go back to the village the critic  argues that while the explicit bullying  makes for easy conflict and also feels a  little dumbed down the others on the  show agreed feeling that while the  overall purpose of the scene was fine  the silly dialogue undercuts the tension  saying instead of hokey dialogue it  could have all been done in looks or  different ways just adult it up a little  bit  prey ends much like the original  predator with naru defeating the alien  hunter by utilizing her wits and  escaping with her life some have  complained that nauru should have been  roughed up a bit more during her battle  with the predator noting that even  arnold schwarzenegger was left bloodied  and broken at the end of the original  film one user makes a point that even  after she massacres the alien narut  doesn't have a mark on her they go on to  note that the team from predator had  difficulty bringing down the original  alien even with their high-tech weaponry  a reddit user stated that they enjoyed  prey but added that they missed how  clever the predator used to be they went  on to lament how the predators no longer  seem like much of a threatening presence  after a few movies that have seen them  be beaten with relative ease  an aspect of prey drawing criticism from  fans is the lack of memorable supporting  characters it's almost a tradition for  predator films to feature great  ensembles surrounding the central  protagonist in their battle with the  alien hunter  john mctiernan's original 1987 film  included the likes of carl weathers bill  duke sunny landom and jesse ventura  among others while latter sequels  arguably dipped in quality from the  original hit or missed tv host andrew  tate opined that even the lesser films  had solid supporting casts he argues  prey doesn't have supporting characters  other than the brother the lead  character's brother he's in it i thought  he was really good but he wasn't in it  enough there wasn't enough development  tate felt none of the deaths and prey  really mattered explaining  there's too many other characters that  get wiped out and i'm just like oh well  it's just another generic npc from  skyrim i don't care about them one 4 out  of 10 rating on imdb had a fairly  scathing review stating the comanche  people portrayed in the film have only  one thing to live for survival it also  makes it very hard for them to be  personable and likeable every character  in the film other than the main girl  might as well have been the exact same  person  one of arnold schwarzenegger's most  iconic one-liners comes from the  original predator  if it bleeds  we can kill it  the same line is repeated in prey by  nauru's brother tabe while they're both  tied to a tree during the battle  sequence with the french fur trappers  for some the moment was a  goosebump-inducing callback to predator  but others felt a bit of dialogue was  shoehorned into the film one tweet  described the line as being shoehorned  into prey for no reason in the comment  section below the tweet the user posited  it would have been better if they gave  one of billy's lines to them there's  something hunting us and it ain't no man  we're all gonna die and then they all  indeed die  about midway through prey nauru comes to  a startling conclusion while tied up to  a tree with her brother the predator  won't kill her because it doesn't see  her as a threat this ties into the  overall theme of prey naru is trying to  prove her worth to those around her  while many in her tribe see her is  little more than someone who needs to  learn her place however some fans were  angered by this twist in their negative  review of the film bad movie reviews  claimed the movie constantly panders to  gender politics as apparently in this  movie the predator isn't attacking the  female lead because it doesn't see her  as a threat since when does the predator  care about the gender of its victims in  the comment section for the same video a  user noted that the predator slaughtered  the fatally injured fur trapper raphael  despite knowing that he didn't have a  weapon and was physically hampered he  explains he certainly wasn't a threat  but that didn't stop the predator from  killing him others in the comments agree  with another user arguing don't let  anyone fool you predators have attacked  women with weapons in other movies only  exception was predator 2 where the woman  was pregnant and he didn't  in one particular way prey seems to be  messing with predator franchise lore  which is a bad idea when dealing with  hardcore fandom the character of rafael  attolini plays a huge part in the  franchise at least in terms of comic  books and spin-offs adelini was the name  inscribed on the gun given to danny  glover by one of the departing predators  at the end of predator 2 seemingly as a  sign of respect for years fans wondered  who this mysterious man was and why a  predator would carry around his weapon  clearly seeing it as some sort of prized  trophy to be handed off when vested in  combat as it turns out the answers lie  in a 1996 dark horse comic book titled  predator 1718 a storyline prey  completely ignores  instead the film features a man named  rafael who was killed by the predator  after handing his flintlock pistol to  naru while it's neat to see the predator  2 easter egg and pray the complete  disregard for previous comic book canon  has disappointed some much like disney's  retconning of pre-existing star wars  expanded universe stories  one of the coolest scenes in prey  features naru taking out a group of  french trappers using her throwing axe  and some well-timed flips chantal looked  like one long take the sequence is  violent gory and completely badass as  nauru slices and diced his enemies left  and right without remorse still there  were quite a few fans who decried the  moment as unbelievable a reddit user  noted that nauru was mostly seen as  useless by her tribe for much of the  film continuing  then when the movie calls for it she can  suddenly slaughter a camp of 10 or so  men in 45 seconds it would have been a  better step imo for her to have been a  capable hunter and warrior rather than  making her instantly go into beast mode  for the last 15 to 20 minutes  others have joked that nauru's abilities  are more akin to kiana reeves killer  assassin than john wick than a real-life  indigenous warrior one tweet jokes naru  pray is very obviously the founder of  the assassins guild and john wick the  obvious fact that john wick predator and  alien as a shared universe is basically  the greatest gift 2022 could have given  me  [Music]

